            <div xml:id="d32">

                <pb facs="0039" n="29" sameAs="frus:frus1948v08/pg29"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.24/3–348: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Stuart</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1948-03-04T17:00:00-05:00">March 4, 1948—5 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>345. Action recommended urtel 400 Mar. 3 approved and will be adopted. Chinese
                    Emb has been informed of FLC’s readiness to open negotiations for purchase
                    surplus ammo Hawaii and Pacific. Despite repeated requests by Chinese Emb for
                    surplus ammo and advance notice given Chinese Emb informally of likelihood that
                    ammo in question would be available, Chinese Emb now states that no Chinese rep
                    here empowered to negotiate purchase Hawaii surplus and it is requesting
                    instructions. Please recommend prompt action by FonOff and at same time suggest
                    that Chinese Govt begin making shipping arrangements for moving supplies to
                    China.</p>
                <p>FLC instruction to Luboshez regarding Pacific surplus went forward yesterday.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Marshall</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
